# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 2 of the Tutorial

[AS5's Figure 2.29]

ev,a,0,v
r1,a,c,r1
r2,c,0,r2

analysis: dc
note: Symbolic all through: the answers come back as formulas.
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes
evaluate: -pev


[B11's Example 5.6 - with the Solve equations card]

e,1,0,e
r1,1,2,r1
r2,2,3,4'k
r3,3,0,6'k

analysis: dc
note: Solve the circuit first, then use the Solve equations card.
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes
solve_equations: re = 12000
solve_equations: ir3 = 0.006
solve_unknowns: e, r1


[B11's Example 5.6 - using Expert Mode]

e,1,0,e
r1,1,2,rx
r2,2,3,4'k
r3,3,0,6'k

analysis: dc
note: The same problem, with the two facts handed over before solving.
unknowns: e, rx
equations: re = 12000
equations: ir3 = 0.006
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


